# Why Revived

The Why Revived site, with a public [Wisp](https://github.com/MercuryWorkshop/wisp-protocol/blob/v2/protocol.md) server behind it (v2, and v1 for libcurl.js). Cloudflare publishes the page and the websocket, so both stay reachable without a console attached.

This is basically a web proxy with two backends, 1 is fetch.php 2, is WISP, normally you would make a public wisp using cloudflare.

## Run

```bash
npm install
npm run public
```

That starts the server and a Cloudflare quick tunnel. The page shows the public `wss://…/wisp/` address once the tunnel is up. Restarting the tunnel gives a new address.

To run only the server:

```bash
npm start
```

Then check the handshake, a blocked destination, and a real TCP stream:

```bash
npm run check
```

Open the site at the local server root, or at the `https://….trycloudflare.com` address printed by the tunnel.
